From a98c72728c8136d1de6ad227812d175f10b42f9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio D'Achille <existenz70@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:30:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Ming-Image 0.1 Design: converters, text encoder graph,
 VAE, DiT conditioning (not wired into generation)

Adds ModelVersion.mingImage (the DiT is Z-Image's graph without the learned pad tokens) and
everything needed to convert and run its parts, each checked against a PyTorch reference:

- ModelImporter/Converter/QuantI8x: DiT recognised and converted; 8-bit S (i8x) rule.
- ModelConverter --ming-text-encoder: Ling MoE language model, Qwen2 connector, projections and
  the tokenizer from ComfyUI's single file; QuantI8x --text-encoder keeps routers, embeddings,
  query tokens and the small projections in FP16.
- ModelConverter --ming-vae: the Wan VAE graph with four (RGBA) channels.
- MingText.swift: Ling layer by layer (the host picks the experts inside score groups,
  MoERouting only weights them), connector, directvlm projection, VAE wrappers.
- ZImage.swift: MingImageFixed (queries through cap_embedder plus 3840-wide tokens, no padding)
  and ZImageRotaryPositionEmbedding.imageTimePosition.
- QuantI8x: BFloat16 tensors go through Float (a direct CPU BFloat16 -> Float16 conversion
  returns zeros).
- Test executables MingEncoderTest, MingVAETest, MingDiTTest.

Generation is not wired in: UNetFixedEncoder and TextEncoder stop with an error for .mingImage.
Plan and results: DT Hub docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-23-ming-image-design.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
